Lolly patch 0010: no analytics tag.

Why: upstream's HTML pages (the editor, the docs, cookbook, reference and
troubleshooting pages) load Google Analytics. Lolly ships no trackers
(docs/privacy.md, tests/no-trackers.test.ts). Lolly's editor build does not
use these pages, but the vendored tree should not carry the tag either, so
each block is replaced by a one-line comment.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

diff --git a/packages/app/cookbook.html b/packages/app/cookbook.html
index ac365bb9f02022073b3ab48e818848706f0a0ab4..ae5d6ec9003aaf8c787706289f52242fbefd2593 100644
--- a/packages/app/cookbook.html
+++ b/packages/app/cookbook.html
@@ -1,16 +1,7 @@
 <!doctype html>
 <html lang="en">
   <head>
-    <!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
-    <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-LEDJP5EFLD"></script>
-    <script>
-      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
-      function gtag() {
-        dataLayer.push(arguments);
-      }
-      gtag('js', new Date());
-      gtag('config', 'G-LEDJP5EFLD');
-    </script>
+    <!-- Lolly: upstream's Google Analytics tag removed; Lolly ships no trackers. -->
     <meta charset="UTF-8" />
     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
     <meta name="theme-color" content="#050807" />
